# The unsigned journal from the chest in the well caves: a sanguophage's
# confession, read in the conversation window (the reader's portrait shows).
# Re-readable any time; the item persists. Act 2 foreshadowing: the crypt,
# Old Wick's warm door, Mara's blood-drinkers.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_WeatheredJournal

== start ==
The journal spans decades. The early pages are a young retainer's: drills, postings, the small pride of a first commendation. Then the entries begin to skip years at a time, and the hand never ages.

* [Turn the pages.] -> middle
* [Close the journal.] -> end

== middle ==
"Served three kings from the same shadow. The first knew what I was and used me gently. The second knew and used me hard. The third never knew, and I miss him most."

"Put down the rising at the weirs today. They were farmers. I have written *they were farmers* in this book eleven times in a hundred years and the ink never gets any lighter."

"A man who cannot die does not get to say the work was the times. The times died. I kept going."

* [Read the last entry.] -> last
* [Close the journal.] -> end

== last ==
The last entry is the shortest.

"I have killed for centuries. Farmers at the weirs. A shepherd in this village. More than I can count. I was made for this and I did it well. Now I am done. I am going into the water and I will not come back up. If you are reading this, do what you will with it. I do not care anymore."

It is not signed.

* [Close the journal.] -> end
